BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interpreting AI at Work: Direct Use\, Workplace Support\, and Tech
 nological Displacement Concerns
DTSTART:20260909T150000Z
DTEND:20260909T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T164147Z
UID:cb5f64c3c79ca091a73f440a@systemsmap.antlerboy.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Complexity
DESCRIPTION:Complexity Science Hub\nWhat happens when employees are asked 
 to embrace a technology that may also threaten their jobs? In this talk\, 
 Christos Makridis examines how workers interpret AI at work using the Gall
 up Workplace Panel\, a probability-based longitudinal survey that follows 
 U.S. adults over time and repeatedly measures their use of AI\, workplace 
 experiences\, and expectations about job loss. Drawing on more than 10\nht
 tps://csh.ac.at/events/interpreting-ai-at-work-direct-use-workplace-suppor
 t-and-technological-displacement-concerns/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260905T164147Z
LOCATION:CSH Salon
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://csh.ac.at/events/interpreting-ai-at-work-direct-use-workplace-
 support-and-technological-displacement-concerns/
END:VEVENT
