BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:WEdnesday SALON with Ljubica Nedelkoska: AI and the End of Work (A
 gain)
DTSTART:20260916T180000Z
DTEND:20260916T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T164147Z
UID:95ae062dbc349d5afed89226@systemsmap.antlerboy.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Complexity
DESCRIPTION:Complexity Science Hub\nFrom the dawn of mechanization to the 
 rise of AI\, machines have taken over task after human task – transformi
 ng work\, making us richer\, and testing our ability to adapt. Is this tim
 e different? For as long as we have built machines\, we have built them to
  take over human work. Work did not end. It was transformed: what we do\, 
 how it is organized\, and where it happens. Collectively\, this made us ri
 c\nhttps://csh.ac.at/events/wednesday-salon-with-ljubica-nedelkoska/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260905T164147Z
LOCATION:CSH Salon
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://csh.ac.at/events/wednesday-salon-with-ljubica-nedelkoska/
END:VEVENT
